Reading:

Additive associativity is insensitive to every axis varied here.
Multiplicative associativity and distributivity are insensitive to
the OVERFLOW axis and sensitive to the FRACTION axis, breaking as
soon as F > 0 and never at F = 0.

So 'the strategy changes what the correct answer is' is true, and it
is true through one specific axis rather than through the marker as a
whole. A strategy that fixes rounding fixes which rewrites are legal.
A strategy that fixes overflow does not touch that question at all.
Two things wearing one name, distinguished by a measurement.
